//
// Phase G's width wall, and the derivation that closes it. Host-only: this
// builds air.ir.Modules and hashes them, and never reaches a device.
//
// THE WALL. `builders.block.norm_rows` is DERIVED per width and says so in its
// own docstring -- the L1 cap moves with emb_dim, so a row count that fit at
// one width is a placement failure at the next. `build_layer_norm_module`'s
// `rows_per_call` was the other half of the same sum and was NOT derived: it
// defaulted to 8, which with herd_x = 8 silently requires 64 | rows. At
// emb_dim 1024 norm_rows derives 32, so `runlist` refused to build at EVERY
// sequence length -- 0 of 9 ladder points against 9 of 9 at 512 and 768
// (doc 50 section 7, found by devq 307 and left unfixed deliberately).
//
// With 32 rows over 8 columns each core owns 4, so a rows_per_call of 4 was
// legal all along. The repair is to DERIVE the parameter, bounded above by the
// historical default.
//
// WHY THE CEILING IS THE WHOLE ARGUMENT. Doc 50 declined to fix this because
// "every plausible repair changes what a `runlist` row means" -- correct, and
// the reason a mode's row is only comparable across widths if its dispatch
// structure is unchanged. A derivation that may only go DOWN from 8 cannot
// move any shape where 8 was legal, and this suite asserts that as BYTE
// EQUALITY over the emitted module at five shapes rather than as an argument
// about it. [23 section 5] records a structural check missing the very claim
// its phase rested on; byte equality covers every axis such a check could name
// and every one it could forget.
//
// The byte-identity clause is paired with its discrimination control -- a
// module built at rows_per_call 4 must DIFFER from one built at 8, or the
// equality above would hold no matter what the derivation returned. And the
// wall itself is pinned as still real: an EXPLICIT rows_per_call of 8 at 32
// rows must still raise, which is what separates "derive the parameter" from
// "delete the constraint". The divisibility rule is a property of the herd
// walk, not a formality: without it a core steps past its own rows.
//
// RUN: python3 %S/builders/test_layer_norm_rows.py | FileCheck %s
// CHECK: layer-norm row tests: 9/9 passed
